Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction to Manipulate[...]", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.38959970931*^9, 3.389599731852*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The single command ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " lets you create an astonishing range of interactive applications with just \
a few lines of input. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " is designed to be used by anyone who is comfortable using basic commands \
such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Plot",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Plot"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ": it does not require learning any complicated new concepts, nor any \
understanding of user interface programing ideas.\n\nThe output you get from \
evaluating a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " command is an interactive object containing one or more controls (sliders, \
etc.) that you can use to vary the value of one or more parameters. The \
output is very much like a small applet or widget: it is not just a static \
result, it is a running program you can interact with.\n\nAt its most basic, \
the syntax of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " is identical to that of the humble function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ". \n\nConsider this ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " command, which produces a list of numbers from 1 to 20 in steps of 1."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389599654104*^9, 3.389599658648*^9}, {3.389599817123*^9,
   3.389599828992*^9}, {3.389606698573*^9, 3.3896067102799997`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{"n", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", "1", ",", "20", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389599948332*^9, 3.389599949031*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nSimply replace the word ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " with the word ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ", and you get an interactive application that lets you explore values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI",
   FontWeight->"Bold"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["20",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " in steps of ",
 StyleBox["1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with a ",
 StyleBox["slider",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3896489290028*^9, 3.3896489381638002`*^9}, 
   3.439069427671875*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Manipulate", "[", 
  RowBox[{"n", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", "1", ",", "20", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389599933547*^9, 3.389599934394*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nMove the above ",
 StyleBox["Slider bar",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and see what happens.\n\nOf course the whole point of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " (and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " for that matter) is that you can put ",
 StyleBox["any",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " expression you like into the first argument, not just a simple variable \
name. \n\nOne way to think of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " is as a way to interactively explore a large parameter space. You can move \
around that space at will, exploring interesting directions as they appear. \n\
\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " supports a wide range of alternate ways of specifying variables, which \
generate different kinds of controls for those variables. These dynamic \
controls include ",
 StyleBox["checkboxes",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["popup menus",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and others in addition to ",
 StyleBox["sliders",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". \n\nThe principle is that for each Dynamic variable, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["u",
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ", you ask for a particular set of possible values for the variable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["u",
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " (like from ",
 StyleBox["1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["20",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " in steps of ",
 StyleBox["1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " e.g. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", "1", ",", "20", ",", "1"}], "}"}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ") and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Manipulate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Manipulate"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["automatically chooses",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " an appropriate type of control to make those values conveniently \
available.\n\n\t",
 StyleBox["Possible Values that you want:\tManipulate Automatically Chooses \
an Appropriate Type of Control:",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["min", "TI"]], ",", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["max", "TI"]]}], "}"}], " "}
    }], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t\tcontinuous manipulator (slider, animator, etc.)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["min", "TI"]], ",", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["max", "TI"]], ",", 
        StyleBox["du", "TI"]}], "}"}], "   "}
    }], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[Cell[TextData[{
    "discrete manipulator with step ",
    Cell[BoxData[
     StyleBox["du", "TI"]], "InlineFormula"]
   }], "TableText"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["min", "TI"]], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["min", "TI"]]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["max", "TI"]], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["max", "TI"]]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t2D slider\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
     ButtonBox["Locator",
      BaseStyle->"Link",
      ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Locator"]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[Cell["a locator in a graphic", "TableText"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["1", "TR"]], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["2", "TR"]], ",", 
       StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]", "TR"]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\t\t\tsetter bar for few elements; popup menu for more\n\tetc.\t\t\t\t\t\
etc.\n\tetc.\t\t\t\t\tetc."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389600685666*^9, 3.3896006894639997`*^9}, {
   3.389600854349*^9, 3.389600862738*^9}, 3.389600927474*^9, {
   3.389601646949*^9, 3.389601689881*^9}, {3.3896017394449997`*^9, 
   3.389601764225*^9}, {3.389601869466*^9, 3.389601874315*^9}, {
   3.389601915804*^9, 3.389601962358*^9}, {3.3896020021689997`*^9, 
   3.3896021412679996`*^9}, {3.389602208443*^9, 3.389602232866*^9}, 
